# The additional cost is paid before the spell resolves (CR 601.2h): Bot1 targets its own Chromatic Star and sacrifices it to pay, so the
# target is gone on resolution and the Rite does nothing (CR 608.2b), though the Star's "put into a graveyard from the battlefield" trigger
# still draws a card (the hand ends at 5 with it, one more than without). The Rite goes to the graveyard, castable again with flashback.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Swamp
Chromatic Star
Rite of Oblivion
Plains x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Chromatic Star.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Rite of Oblivion.Cast(Chromatic Star)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Rite of Oblivion; Chromatic Star
Bot1.Hand.Count = 5
Exile.Count = 0
